            <ArticleTitle>Utility of stress echocardiography in the triage of patients with atypical chest pain from the emergency department.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1282-4, A10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We followed 108 patients presenting to the emergency department with atypical chest pain and triaged with stress echocardiography. One-year cardiac event-free survival was 100% with a negative stress echocardiogram and 25% with a positive study.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
